{"ts": 1792272361.813293, "kind": "feedback", "entry": "fb_9c2b1f03", "subject_kind": "item", "subject": "docs/courses/state-layer/selectors.md", "office": "cto", "by": "cmo research", "comment": "The lesson says Reselect's cache holds only the last call. In Reselect 5 (used by Redux Toolkit 2) the default memoize is weakMapMemoize, which keeps an entry per set of arguments; the single-entry lruMemoize is an option. Correct the lesson and cite the Reselect 5 docs."}
{"ts": 1792272362.2061636, "kind": "feedback", "entry": "fb_9afbc409", "subject_kind": "item", "subject": "docs/practice/memoized-selector.md", "office": "cto", "by": "cmo research", "comment": "The question's explanation says Reselect's cache holds only the last call. In Reselect 5 the default memoize (weakMapMemoize) keeps an entry per set of arguments; lruMemoize with maxSize 1 is the old behaviour. Correct the explanation without changing the question's tests."}
